Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- An unpinned thread card (the card variant of SidebarThreadRow: Active and Working cards in the ungrouped list and the cards inside project folders in the grouped sidebar) shows a Pin button in the pin slot, between the project favicon and the project name, where a pinned card shows its pin icon that turns into the Unpin button on hover.
- The button is shown only when the thread is not pinned, pinning is supported (server config loaded), the user can operate the thread and the row is not being dragged. It appears while the row is hovered (the group-any-hover/sidebar-row variant the card's other hover controls use) and while the row or a control in it has keyboard focus; otherwise it is display: none and takes no space, so the project name sits where it does today and moves right by the icon's width plus the header gap (18px) only while the button shows. No animation is added; only the hover colour change the Unpin button already has.
- It has the Unpin button's size, colour and hover colour (PinIcon size-3, text-muted-foreground/65, hover:text-foreground), with tooltip and aria-label "Pin thread" (gt() for the label, <T> for the tooltip, as the Unpin button does).
- Clicking it pins the thread exactly as the context menu's Pin thread does: SidebarThreadRow gets an onPin prop, wired to Sidebar's existing attemptPin (pinThread plus the "Failed to pin thread" toast). The click calls preventDefault and stopPropagation so the row does not navigate; pointerdown stops propagation like the Snooze trigger and Discard draft, so pressing it never starts a row drag or the sweep gesture. A double-click on it does not start a rename, because the row ignores double-clicks on buttons.
- The slim rows (Snoozed, Settled) and the folder and folder-multiline variants are unchanged; in the grouped sidebar a folder card is a card, so it shows the button and pinning it moves the thread from its folder to the pinned cards, as the menu does. Touch-only screens (no hover) keep pinning from the context menu.
- The new copy is wrapped for gt-react (docs/internals/i18n.md) with its English text byte-identical; the translation catalogs are not changed, so the missing <T>Pin thread</T> key renders the English source.
- The user guide's Pin and reorder threads section mentions the pin button that appears when you hover a card.

